      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has identical rows\n- $A$ has proportional columns\n- $A$ has a zero row",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
